course: dictionary
lesson: 10571
title: Slang and informal words
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words belong to informal talk, the way friends speak to each other. Uncool is slang, so you would hear it in a playground or a chat with friends, not in a formal letter or a school report. When you meet slang, look at the words around it for clues, just as you would with any new word.
explain: «It's not uncool to ask for a bedtime; it helps.» The word not is a big clue. Uncool is the opposite of cool, so the sentence means asking for a bedtime is not embarrassing in front of friends, and it helps you. Try your meaning in the sentence: "It's not embarrassing to ask for a bedtime; it helps." It still makes sense, so you have the right meaning.
explain: Uncool has a second meaning too: not fair or not kind. Someone might say, «That was really uncool of you», meaning that was mean. The words around it tell you which meaning fits. Is the sentence about clothes or fashion, or about how someone behaved?
fact: Uncool is slang, so it is informal: friends use it when they talk, but it is not used in formal writing.
fact: «Uncool» means not fashionable or not stylish, and it can make you feel embarrassed in front of friends.
fact: «Uncool» can also mean not fair or not kind, as in «That was really uncool of you.»
fact: Cool is the opposite of uncool, so the word cool can help you work out what uncool means.
fact: Slang can be hard to understand if you are not in the group that uses it, so a dictionary is a good check when you are not sure.
exercise: «It's not uncool to ask for a bedtime; it helps.» What does uncool mean in this sentence? | Rude to parents | Very tired | Loud and noisy | *Embarrassing in front of friends
exercise: «That was really uncool of you.» What does uncool mean here? | *Not fair or not kind | Very fashionable | Cold and icy | Funny and silly
exercise: Which word is informal slang, the kind of word friends use when they chat? | consequently | *uncool | ancient | furthermore
test: Jade says, «My mum's jumper is so uncool.» What is she most likely saying? | Her mum is a famous singer | Her mum's jumper is very warm and cosy | *Her mum's jumper is not stylish or fashionable | Her mum has bought a new car
test: «Taking the last biscuit without asking was uncool.» What does uncool suggest? | Very tasty | A sign of a hot day | Tired after a long day | *Not fair or not kind
exam: In «It's not uncool to ask for a bedtime; it helps», which meaning of uncool fits best? | *Embarrassing in front of friends | Rude and loud | Soft and quiet | Hot and sunny
